luation","slug":"monitoring_and_evaluation","type":"overview","sources":["Climate Watch"]},"64372":{"name":"Co-benefits","slug":"cobenefits","type":"overview","sources":["Climate Watch"]},"64373":{"name":"International Frameworks","slug":"international_frameworks","type":"overview","sources":["Climate Watch"]},"64374":{"name":"Gender and Indigenous People","slug":"gender_and_indigenous_people","type":"overview","sources":["Climate Watch"]},"64375":{"name":"Loss and Damage","slug":"loss_and_damage","type":"overview","sources":["Climate Watch"]},"64376":{"name":"Loss and Damage","slug":"loss_and_damage","type":"map","sources":["Climate Watch"]},"64377":{"name":"Transformative Adaptation","slug":"transformative_adaptation","type":"overview","sources":["Climate Watch"]},"64378":{"name":"Transformative Adaptation","slug":"transformative_adaptation","type":"map","sources":["Climate Watch"]},"64379":{"name":"Children and Young People","slug":"children_and_young_people","type":"overview","sources":["UNICEF"]},"64380":{"name":"Vulnerability","slug":"vulnerability","type":"overview","sources":["UNICEF","NDC Explorer"]},"64381":{"name":"Climate Risks","slug":"climate_risks","type":"overview","sources":["NDC Explorer"]},"64382":{"name":"Mitigation: GHG Target Type","slug":"mitigation_ghg_target_type","type":"map","sources":["Climate Watch"]},"64383":{"name":"Mitigation: Sector Coverage","slug":"mitigation_sector_coverage","type":"map","sources":["Climate Watch"]},"64384":{"name":"Mitigation: Gas Coverage","slug":"mitigation_gas_coverage","type":"map","sources":["Climate Watch"]},"64385":{"name":"Fairness, Ambition and Objective","slug":"fairness_ambition_and_objective","type":"overview","sources":["Climate Watch"]}},"sectors":{},"indicators":[{"id":648348,"source":"Climate Watch","name":"NDC summary","slug":"indc_summary","grouping_indicator":false,"category_ids":[64321,64324],"labels":{},"locations":{"KEN":[{"value":"\"Kenya aims to implement mitigation measures to achieve absolute emission reductions of 75 MtCO2eq by 2035. Out of the 75 MtCO2eq, unconditional measures are expected to lead to a 15 MtCO2eq emission reduction amount. An additional 60 MtCO2eq emission reduction is achievable if support is made available from international sources to cover the full cost for implementation.\"","document_slug":"second_ndc","group_index":null},{"value":"“Kenya seeks to undertake an ambitious mitigation contribution towards the Paris Agreement. Kenya therefore seeks to abate her GHG emissions by 32% by 2030 relative to the BAU scenario of 143 MtCO\u003csub\u003e2\u003c/sub\u003eeq; and in line with her sustainable development agenda. Kenya commits to bear 21% of the mitigation costs from domestic sources, while 79% of this is subject to international support in the form of finance, investment, technology development and transfer, and capacity building.”\u003cbr\u003e\"Kenya\u0026rsquo;s Updated NDC includes both mitigation and adaptation components based on her national circumstances and in line with decisions 1/CP.19 and 1/CP.20.\"","document_slug":"revised_first_ndc","group_index":null},{"value":"Kenya seeks to undertake an ambitious mitigation contribution towards the 2015 Agreement. Kenya therefore seeks to abate its GHG emissions by 30% by 2030 relative to the BAU scenario of 143 MtCO\u003csub\u003e2\u003c/sub\u003eeq; and in line with its sustainable development agenda. This is also subject to international support in the form of finance, investment, technology development and transfer, and capacity building.\u003cbr /\u003e\"Kenya\u0026rsquo;s INDC includes both mitigation and adaptation components based on her national circumstances and in line with decisions 1/CP.19 and 1/CP.20. \"","document_slug":"first_ndc","group_index":null},{"value":"Kenya seeks to undertake an ambitious mitigation contribution towards the 2015 Agreement. Kenya therefore seeks to abate its GHG emissions by 30% by 2030 relative to the BAU scenario of 143 MtCO\u003csub\u003e2\u003c/sub\u003eeq; and in line with its sustainable development agenda. This is also subject to international support in the form of finance, investment, technology development and transfer, and capacity building.\u003cbr /\u003e\"Kenya\u0026rsquo;s INDC includes both mitigation and adaptation components based on her national circumstances and in line with decisions 1/CP.19 and 1/CP.20. \"","document_slug":"indc","group_index":null}]}},{"id":648353,"source":"Climate Watch","name":"GHG target","slug":"ghg_target","grouping_indicator":false,"category_ids":[64321,64326],"labels":{},"locations":{"KEN":[{"value":"Kenya commits to reduce its emissions by 75 MtCO2e (15 unconditional, 60 conditional), compared to BAU by 2035.","document_slug":"second_ndc","group_index":null},{"value":"32% reduction in GHG emissions by 2030 compared to BAU scenario (143 MtCO2eq)","document_slug":"revised_first_ndc","group_index":null},{"value":"30% reduction in GHG emissions by 2030 compared to BAU scenario (143 MtCO2eq)","document_slug":"first_ndc","group_index":null},{"value":"30% reduction in GHG emissions by 2030 compared to BAU scenario (143 MtCO2eq)","document_slug":"indc","group_index":null}]}},{"id":648356,"source":"Climate Watch","name":"Target year (mitigation)","slug":"time_target_year","grouping_indicator":false,"category_ids":[64321,64324,64325],"labels":{"1283659":{"name":"2025","slug":null,"index":1},"1283660":{"name":"2030","slug":null,"index":2},"1283661":{"name":"2035","slug":null,"index":3},"1283662":{"name":"2040","slug":null,"index":4},"1283663":{"name":"2025 and 2030","slug":null,"index":5},"1283664":{"name":"2030 and 2035","slug":null,"index":6},"1283665":{"name":"Other","slug":null,"index":7},"1283666":{"name":"Not Applicable","slug":null,"index":8},"1283667":{"name":"No Document Submitted","slug":null,"index":-2}},"locations":{"KEN":[{"value":"2035","label_id":1283661,"document_slug":"second_ndc","group_index":null},{"value":"The timeframe for implementati